    [Feature][PCP] Support fixed-K speculative decode request sharding (#18112)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Enable PCP decode request sharding with fixed-K speculative decoding.
    The target uses PCP sharding while the draft continues to run a
    replicated global batch.
    
    - Expose consistent global token extents, request boundaries and hidden
    states at the PCP restoration boundary while preserving the target's
    graph inputs.
    - Pad FULL MLA/GQA draft metadata for DP dummy execution as well as real
    requests; both CPU and GPU query boundaries cover the selected graph.
    - Rebuild global draft attention metadata for sharded MLA/GQA targets
    using FULL graphs. Describe graph padding with zero-KV dummy requests
    and keep CPU/GPU query boundaries consistent.
    - Synchronize replicated DSpark draft batches independently across DP
    ranks, matching the existing MTP/Eagle behavior.
    - Preallocate the DeepSeek V4 MTP residual buffer before compilation so
    graph replay and draft restoration use the same storage.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Fixed-K speculative decoding can use PCP decode sharding with
    supported graph modes. No new configuration options are introduced. The
    draft remains replicated.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Latest revision `0a524ae30`, rebased onto main `7fa6b34dc`: initialize
    replicated_pcp=False in the DCP speculator test fixture, which bypasses
    __init__. The previous CPU CI failure was reproduced as 19 failing
    cases; all 281 related tests passed remotely after the one-line fixture
    repair and rebase. No additional runtime change was made for this CI
    failure. Latest CI is pending.
    
    - Latest update `9fd91c25e`: reproduced a DP2 x TP2 x PCP2 MLA/MTP
    FULL-graph failure in runtime dummy execution (`actual_seq_lengths=8`,
    query T=16). After the fix, both FULL_DECODE_ONLY and eager completed
    balanced (4/4 requests), uneven with an idle DP rank (1/4), and mixed
    queued batches (7/3). Target and draft graph replay were observed. Small
    random dummy-weight model, fixed-K=3, input lengths 1-960; functional
    coverage only.
    - All 243 relevant remote unit tests passed, including dummy-padding
    CPU/GPU boundary consistency and existing real-request regressions.
    Latest CI is pending.
    
    - Latest update `c2b5263a4` rebased onto main `03f31cfb8`: 238 relevant
    unit tests passed remotely. Before the fix, the DSpark regression
    reproduced the upstream assertion when four global draft requests reused
    a target sync covering two requests; the non-PCP control passed.
    - A remote two-process Gloo probe passed balanced, uneven, idle-rank and
    eager-fallback DP synchronization cases using the upstream dispatch
    helper. Graph selection was mocked; this is not an end-to-end DSpark NPU
    model inference test. DSpark multi-DP NPU model execution remains
    unverified; the MLA/MTP coverage is described above.
    - CI for the latest update is queued; the results below refer to the
    previous revision.
    
    - All CI checks passed on `f879386ed`: 31 successful checks and 5
    skipped checks, including CPU unit tests for vLLM main and `v0.30.0` and
    the selected NPU tests.
    - 185 relevant unit tests passed in a remote Ascend container:
    
      ```bash
      pytest -q tests/ut/worker/test_pcp_manager_v2.py \
        tests/ut/worker/test_mtp_pcp_speculator_v2.py \
        tests/ut/worker/v2/test_speculator.py
      ```
    
    - Remote MLA/MTP regression tests passed with PCP sharding in both
    `FULL_DECODE_ONLY` (capture sizes `[8, 16]`) and eager mode: short
    single request, long single request, mixed three requests and mixed
    seven requests. The original FIA query-length mismatch did not recur.
    These tests used a small random model with dummy weights and validate
    functional execution and metadata layout, not numerical accuracy.
    - Local Ruff and diff checks passed.
    
    The remote runtime used [vLLM commit
    ced6857](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607).
    The latest parent-restoration refactor was checked with the 185 unit
    tests; the preceding production revision passed the MLA runtime cases
    above. Earlier real-model comparisons had unresolved mixed-batch output
    differences, so complete numerical equivalence is not claimed.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
